{
 "as_of": "2026-10-06",
 "descriptor": "Lubricant additives, rubber chemicals and aroma chemicals",
 "lede": "A Vapi chemical maker whose big new Pakhajan plant crushed profits for two years under interest and depreciation, and has now started to fill: Q1 FY27 revenue rose 56% and the EBITDA margin jumped to 24%. If that margin holds, earnings re-rate sharply; if Q1 was a peak, the stock at ~99x trailing earnings has far to fall.",
 "market": {
  "price": 4283,
  "mcap_cr": 5163,
  "pe": 98.7,
  "pb": 11.7,
  "ev_ebitda": 32
 },
 "short_version": [
  {
   "lead": "What's going right",
   "text": "Q1 FY27 revenue ₹308 Cr (+56%) on 42% higher volumes, EBITDA margin 24.2% (from ~17%), PAT ₹36 Cr against ₹21 Cr for all of FY26. Net debt/EBITDA fell to 1.86x, working capital to 143 days, ratings upgraded to A-, and a 15-year MNC supply contract starts in FY28."
  },
  {
   "lead": "What to be sceptical about",
   "text": "One quarter of 24% margins against a 15-17% history, partly helped by April price rises; capex doubled to ₹250 Cr with ~₹100 Cr of new debt; ROCE was 7-8% in FY25-26. Three family directors are paid 45-60x the median employee."
  },
  {
   "lead": "Price",
   "text": "~99x trailing earnings but ~32x EV/EBITDA; Vinati Organics trades at 27x, NOCIL at 41x."
  }
 ],
 "sections": [
  {
   "id": "business",
   "title": "Company overview and business model",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": "Yasho makes specialty chemicals in Gujarat: lubricant additives, rubber antioxidants and accelerators, and other industrial chemicals (87-89% of revenue), plus a smaller food and aroma chemicals line. It sells pure chemicals, not formulations, to global lubricant and rubber majors, with subsidiaries in Europe and the US. A second plant at Pakhajan (commissioned FY25) multiplied capacity.",
     "src": "May call p.8"
    },
    {
     "type": "tiles",
     "items": [
      {
       "value": "62-69%",
       "label": "Exports share of revenue"
      },
      {
       "value": "~65%",
       "label": "Utilisation in Q1 FY27 (75% targeted)"
      },
      {
       "value": "₹51.4 Cr",
       "label": "Advance from an MNC under a 15-year supply deal"
      },
      {
       "value": "~7%",
       "label": "Revenue from the largest customer"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "bullets",
     "title": "Where the profit comes from",
     "items": [
      {
       "lead": "",
       "text": "New products launched in the last year earn ~10-12 points more margin than older ones.",
       "src": "Aug call p.16"
      },
      {
       "lead": "",
       "text": "More than half of revenue is now on formula-based quarterly or six-monthly pricing, which keeps the EBITDA percentage stable.",
       "src": "Aug call p.10"
      },
      {
       "lead": "",
       "text": "Utilisation drives margins: fixed costs of the Pakhajan plant spread over more volume.",
       "src": "Aug call p.7"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "bullets",
     "title": "What changed in 3–5 years",
     "items": [
      {
       "lead": "",
       "text": "Revenue from ₹614 Cr (FY22) to ₹817 Cr (FY26, standalone); FY24 dipped 11%.",
       "src": null
      },
      {
       "lead": "",
       "text": "Pakhajan plant and R&D centre (50+ scientists) built with debt; borrowings rose from ₹179 Cr to ~₹580 Cr.",
       "src": null
      },
      {
       "lead": "",
       "text": "Shut R&D at Vapi and moved it to Pakhajan; Vapi plant runs near full.",
       "src": "Aug call p.14"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
